{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response","hook_id":"66a934e4-a401-4c4a-81c1-d178d4ceb1d6","hook_name":"SessionStart:startup","hook_event":"SessionStart","output":"  [Token Optimizer v5.2.0] Windows support is now live.\r\n  v5.1.0 hooks ran via POSIX shell and failed silently on Windows;\r\n  v5.2.0 uses a cross-platform wrapper so everything now works.\r\n  Verify with: python3 \"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\token-optimizer\\skills\\token-optimizer\\scripts\\measure.py\" health-selfcheck\r\n\r\n  ====================================================================\r\n  Token Optimizer v5: Active Compression\r\n  ====================================================================\r\n\r\n  Hi! Token Optimizer just got smarter. It can now actively reduce\r\n  the tokens your sessions use -- not just measure them.\r\n\r\n  Here's what's new. You can turn any of these on or off anytime\r\n  from the dashboard (token-dashboard) or with the command:\r\n    measure.py v5 enable <feature>\r\n    measure.py v5 disable <feature>\r\n\r\n  [ON] Quality Nudges (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Warns you when your context quality drops suddenly (e.g., from 85 to 60).\r\n       Risk: None. Only adds a short warning to context, never removes anything.\r\n\r\n  [ON] Loop Detection (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Detects when the AI is stuck retrying the same thing and warns you.\r\n       Risk: None. Only adds a short warning to context, never removes anything.\r\n\r\n  [ON] Delta Mode (Smart Re-reads) (recommended)\r\n       What it does: When the AI re-reads a file after editing it, shows only what changed instead of the whole file.\r\n       Risk: Low. If the AI needed the full file to understand the change in context, the diff alone might not be enough. This is why we fall back to full re-read on large changes (>1500 chars) and big files (>2000 lines).\r\n\r\n  [OFF] Structure Map Measurement (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Logs compression events when structure map fires, so you can track actual savings via compression-stats.\r\n       Risk: None. Local SQLite writes only. The actual substitution is controlled by the read-cache mode, not this flag.\r\n\r\n  [ON] Bash Output Compression (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Rewrites 'git status', 'pytest', 'npm install' etc. to return compressed summaries instead of verbose output.\r\n       Risk: Low. Compression is lossy by design: 'git diff' truncates to 30 lines on large diffs, 'pytest' shows pass/fail counts but strips individual passing tests, 'git log' drops merge commit details. For routine checks this is fine. For careful diff review or debugging specific test failures, set TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_BASH_COMPRESS=0 to disable temporarily.\r\n\r\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  DEFAULTS (what's on right now):\r\n    - Quality Nudges      ON  (harmless, just warnings)\r\n    - Loop Detection      ON  (harmless, just warnings)\r\n    - Delta Mode          ON  (smart re-reads, big savings)\r\n    - Bash Compression    ON  (lossy, disable: TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_BASH_COMPRESS=0)\r\n    - Structure Map        ON  (soft-block, measurement: TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_STRUCTURE_MAP=beta)\r\n\r\n  Want to change these? Three ways:\r\n    1. Dashboard:  token-dashboard  (visit the Manage tab)\r\n    2. CLI:        measure.py v5 enable|disable <feature>\r\n    3. Env var:    TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_<NAME>=0 in your shell\r\n\r\n  Full docs: measure.py v5 info <feature>\r\n  All your data stays 100% local on your machine.\r\n\r\n[Token Optimizer] Quality bar already fully installed.\r\n","stdout":"  [Token Optimizer v5.2.0] Windows support is now live.\r\n  v5.1.0 hooks ran via POSIX shell and failed silently on Windows;\r\n  v5.2.0 uses a cross-platform wrapper so everything now works.\r\n  Verify with: python3 \"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\token-optimizer\\skills\\token-optimizer\\scripts\\measure.py\" health-selfcheck\r\n\r\n  ====================================================================\r\n  Token Optimizer v5: Active Compression\r\n  ====================================================================\r\n\r\n  Hi! Token Optimizer just got smarter. It can now actively reduce\r\n  the tokens your sessions use -- not just measure them.\r\n\r\n  Here's what's new. You can turn any of these on or off anytime\r\n  from the dashboard (token-dashboard) or with the command:\r\n    measure.py v5 enable <feature>\r\n    measure.py v5 disable <feature>\r\n\r\n  [ON] Quality Nudges (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Warns you when your context quality drops suddenly (e.g., from 85 to 60).\r\n       Risk: None. Only adds a short warning to context, never removes anything.\r\n\r\n  [ON] Loop Detection (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Detects when the AI is stuck retrying the same thing and warns you.\r\n       Risk: None. Only adds a short warning to context, never removes anything.\r\n\r\n  [ON] Delta Mode (Smart Re-reads) (recommended)\r\n       What it does: When the AI re-reads a file after editing it, shows only what changed instead of the whole file.\r\n       Risk: Low. If the AI needed the full file to understand the change in context, the diff alone might not be enough. This is why we fall back to full re-read on large changes (>1500 chars) and big files (>2000 lines).\r\n\r\n  [OFF] Structure Map Measurement (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Logs compression events when structure map fires, so you can track actual savings via compression-stats.\r\n       Risk: None. Local SQLite writes only. The actual substitution is controlled by the read-cache mode, not this flag.\r\n\r\n  [ON] Bash Output Compression (recommended)\r\n       What it does: Rewrites 'git status', 'pytest', 'npm install' etc. to return compressed summaries instead of verbose output.\r\n       Risk: Low. Compression is lossy by design: 'git diff' truncates to 30 lines on large diffs, 'pytest' shows pass/fail counts but strips individual passing tests, 'git log' drops merge commit details. For routine checks this is fine. For careful diff review or debugging specific test failures, set TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_BASH_COMPRESS=0 to disable temporarily.\r\n\r\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  DEFAULTS (what's on right now):\r\n    - Quality Nudges      ON  (harmless, just warnings)\r\n    - Loop Detection      ON  (harmless, just warnings)\r\n    - Delta Mode          ON  (smart re-reads, big savings)\r\n    - Bash Compression    ON  (lossy, disable: TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_BASH_COMPRESS=0)\r\n    - Structure Map        ON  (soft-block, measurement: TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_STRUCTURE_MAP=beta)\r\n\r\n  Want to change these? Three ways:\r\n    1. Dashboard:  token-dashboard  (visit the Manage tab)\r\n    2. CLI:        measure.py v5 enable|disable <feature>\r\n    3. Env var:    TOKEN_OPTIMIZER_<NAME>=0 in your shell\r\n\r\n  Full docs: measure.py v5 info <feature>\r\n  All your data stays 100% local on your machine.\r\n\r\n[Token Optimizer] Quality bar already fully installed.\r\n","stderr":"","exit_code":0,"outcome":"success","uuid":"63b55a6b-c97b-46e1-bb38-500f0c7adebe","session_id":"a1f15c39-41f7-448c-b1c6-5d2befa737e7"}
