{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_4992cf6ab3f54b25a69b4987","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## Comprehensive Match-3 Game Project Analysis\n\n### Complete File List\n\n**Project Structure:**\n```\nD:/game-projects/douyin-match3/\n├── index.html                    # Entry point and canvas setup\n├── GDD.md                       # Game Design Document (detailed)\n├── package.json                 # Project configuration\n└── src/\n    ├── assets/                   # Empty directory (planned for assets)\n    ├── css/                      # Empty directory (planned for styles)\n    └── js/\n        ├── Animation.js          # Easing functions, tween system, particles\n        ├── Board.js              # 8x8 grid state management\n        ├── Game.js               # Main game loop and state machine\n        ├── InputHandler.js      # Touch/mouse input handling\n        ├── MatchEngine.js       # Match detection and special tiles\n        ├── Renderer.js          # Canvas 2D rendering engine\n        └── ScoreSystem.js       # Score calculation and level goals\n```\n\n### Module Responsibilities\n\n#### 1. **Game.js** - Main Game Controller\n- **Role**: Orchestrates the entire game, manages state machine, coordinates all modules\n- **Key Classes**: `Game`, `STATES` (enum for game states)\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `_handleSwap()` - Processes tile swaps and initiates match detection\n  - `_processChain()` - Handles cascading matches and combos\n  - `_loop()` - Main game loop with requestAnimationFrame\n  - `render()` - Coordinates rendering of all game elements\n- **Game States**: MENU, IDLE, SWAPPING, MATCHING, REMOVING, DROPPING, RESULT\n\n#### 2. **Board.js** - Grid State Management\n- **Role**: Manages the 8x8 game grid, tile operations, and match detection\n- **Key Classes**: `Board`, `Tile`, constants for board dimensions and special tiles\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `findAllMatches()` - Detects horizontal/vertical matches of 3+\n  - `findLShapeMatches()` - Detects L/T shaped matches for bomb generation\n  - `applyGravity()` - Makes tiles fall down and fills empty spaces\n  - `hasValidMoves()` - Checks for deadlock scenarios\n  - `shuffle()` - Randomizes board when no moves available\n\n#### 3. **MatchEngine.js** - Match Processing System\n- **Role**: Handles match classification, special tile generation, and cascade processing\n- **Key Classes**: `MatchEngine`, `MatchResult`\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `processCascade()` - Full match processing with animations\n  - `_classifyMatches()` - Determines which tiles to remove and special tiles to create\n  - `triggerSpecial()` - Activates special tile effects (striped bombs, etc.)\n  - `isValidSwap()` - Validates if a swap would create matches\n\n#### 4. **Renderer.js** - Canvas Rendering Engine\n- **Role**: Handles all visual rendering using Canvas 2D\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `drawTile()` - Renders individual tiles with fruit emojis and special effects\n  - `drawBackground()` - Renders game board and grid\n  - `drawUI()` - Renders score, moves, and goal progress\n  - `drawResultScreen()` - Renders win/lose screen with stars\n  - Particle and floating text rendering\n\n#### 5. **InputHandler.js** - Input Management\n- **Role**: Processes touch and mouse input for tile swapping\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `_screenToGrid()` - Converts screen coordinates to board positions\n  - `_onPointerDown/Move/Up()` - Handles input events\n  - Determines swipe direction and validates swaps\n\n#### 6. **ScoreSystem.js** - Scoring and Level Management\n- **Role**: Tracks score, moves, level goals, and star ratings\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `useMove()` - Consumes a move and checks for game over\n  - `addScore()` - Adds points with chain multipliers\n  - `isGoalComplete()` - Checks if level objectives are met\n  - `getStarCount()` - Calculates star rating based on score\n\n#### 7. **Animation.js** - Animation System\n- **Role**: Provides tweening and particle effects\n- **Key Classes**: `TweenManager`, `ParticleSystem`, easing functions\n- **Features**:\n  - Smooth tile movements with various easing functions\n  - Particle explosions for tile removals\n  - Floating score text\n\n### Game Architecture Overview\n\nThe game follows a clean architecture pattern with clear separation of concerns:\n\n```\nGame (Controller)\n├── Board (Data Model)\n├── MatchEngine (Logic)\n├── Renderer (View)\n├── InputHandler (Input)\n├── ScoreSystem (Game Rules)\n└── Animation (Effects)\n```\n\n### Key Game Systems\n\n#### 1. **Board/Matching System**\n- 8x8 grid with 6 colored tiles (apple red, banana yellow, blueberry blue, lime green, grape purple, orange)\n- Matches of 3+ tiles trigger removal\n- L/T shaped matches create area bombs\n- 4 matches create striped bombs (horizontal/vertical)\n- 5 matches create rainbow tiles\n- Cascading matches continue until no more matches\n\n#### 2. **Scoring System**\n- Base score: 10 points per tile removed\n- Chain multipliers: 1x (1 chain), 1.5x (2 chains), 2x (3 chains), 2.5x (4+ chains)\n- Combo text feedback for chains\n- Star rating based on score thresholds\n\n#### 3. **Game Loop Flow**\n```\nIDLE → Input Swap → SWAPPING → Match Detection → MATCHING\n    ↓\nTile Removal → REMOVING → Special Effects → DROPPING\n    ↓\nGravity Apply → Check New Matches → If matches: repeat\n    ↓\nNo More Matches → Check Level Goals → RESULT\n```\n\n#### 4. **Special Tile System**\n- **Striped Bombs**: Remove entire row or column\n- **Area Bombs**: Remove 3x3 area around tile\n- **Rainbow Tiles**: Remove all tiles of one color\n- Special tiles are created during matches and triggered on next move\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n- **Rendering**: Pure Canvas 2D with pixel ratio support\n- **Input**: Touch and mouse event handling with swipe detection\n- **Animation**: Custom tween system with multiple easing functions\n- **Particles**: Custom particle system for visual effects\n- **Performance**: Optimized for 60fps with minimal draw calls\n- **Platform**: Designed for Douyin Mini Game platform (HTML5/CSS3/JS)\n\nThe codebase is well-structured, modular, and implements core match-3 mechanics with room for expansion (obstacles, special goals, social features as outlined in GDD.md). The architecture supports easy addition of new features while maintaining clean separation of concerns."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4fc1920c-0b5c-4266-b43d-05c38f749fa3","uuid":"3e112315-1759-40ca-a1ef-58bb049f7aba","timestamp":"2026-05-22T21:24:40.252Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the match-3 game project at D:/game-projects/douyin-match3/. I need a comprehensive understanding of the codebase:\n\n1. List all files in the project\n2. Read index.html to understand the entry point\n3. Read the main game modules: src/js/Board.js, src/js/MatchEngine.js, src/js/Renderer.js, src/js/InputHandler.js, src/js/ScoreSystem.js and any other JS files\n4. Read the GDD.md if it exists\n5. Understand the game architecture, class structure, and how modules interact\n\nReport back: complete file list, each module's responsibilities, key classes/functions, the game loop flow, and how the board/matching/scoring systems work together.","agentId":"a434640aa7982a2c9","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## Comprehensive Match-3 Game Project Analysis\n\n### Complete File List\n\n**Project Structure:**\n```\nD:/game-projects/douyin-match3/\n├── index.html                    # Entry point and canvas setup\n├── GDD.md                       # Game Design Document (detailed)\n├── package.json                 # Project configuration\n└── src/\n    ├── assets/                   # Empty directory (planned for assets)\n    ├── css/                      # Empty directory (planned for styles)\n    └── js/\n        ├── Animation.js          # Easing functions, tween system, particles\n        ├── Board.js              # 8x8 grid state management\n        ├── Game.js               # Main game loop and state machine\n        ├── InputHandler.js      # Touch/mouse input handling\n        ├── MatchEngine.js       # Match detection and special tiles\n        ├── Renderer.js          # Canvas 2D rendering engine\n        └── ScoreSystem.js       # Score calculation and level goals\n```\n\n### Module Responsibilities\n\n#### 1. **Game.js** - Main Game Controller\n- **Role**: Orchestrates the entire game, manages state machine, coordinates all modules\n- **Key Classes**: `Game`, `STATES` (enum for game states)\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `_handleSwap()` - Processes tile swaps and initiates match detection\n  - `_processChain()` - Handles cascading matches and combos\n  - `_loop()` - Main game loop with requestAnimationFrame\n  - `render()` - Coordinates rendering of all game elements\n- **Game States**: MENU, IDLE, SWAPPING, MATCHING, REMOVING, DROPPING, RESULT\n\n#### 2. **Board.js** - Grid State Management\n- **Role**: Manages the 8x8 game grid, tile operations, and match detection\n- **Key Classes**: `Board`, `Tile`, constants for board dimensions and special tiles\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `findAllMatches()` - Detects horizontal/vertical matches of 3+\n  - `findLShapeMatches()` - Detects L/T shaped matches for bomb generation\n  - `applyGravity()` - Makes tiles fall down and fills empty spaces\n  - `hasValidMoves()` - Checks for deadlock scenarios\n  - `shuffle()` - Randomizes board when no moves available\n\n#### 3. **MatchEngine.js** - Match Processing System\n- **Role**: Handles match classification, special tile generation, and cascade processing\n- **Key Classes**: `MatchEngine`, `MatchResult`\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `processCascade()` - Full match processing with animations\n  - `_classifyMatches()` - Determines which tiles to remove and special tiles to create\n  - `triggerSpecial()` - Activates special tile effects (striped bombs, etc.)\n  - `isValidSwap()` - Validates if a swap would create matches\n\n#### 4. **Renderer.js** - Canvas Rendering Engine\n- **Role**: Handles all visual rendering using Canvas 2D\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `drawTile()` - Renders individual tiles with fruit emojis and special effects\n  - `drawBackground()` - Renders game board and grid\n  - `drawUI()` - Renders score, moves, and goal progress\n  - `drawResultScreen()` - Renders win/lose screen with stars\n  - Particle and floating text rendering\n\n#### 5. **InputHandler.js** - Input Management\n- **Role**: Processes touch and mouse input for tile swapping\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `_screenToGrid()` - Converts screen coordinates to board positions\n  - `_onPointerDown/Move/Up()` - Handles input events\n  - Determines swipe direction and validates swaps\n\n#### 6. **ScoreSystem.js** - Scoring and Level Management\n- **Role**: Tracks score, moves, level goals, and star ratings\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `useMove()` - Consumes a move and checks for game over\n  - `addScore()` - Adds points with chain multipliers\n  - `isGoalComplete()` - Checks if level objectives are met\n  - `getStarCount()` - Calculates star rating based on score\n\n#### 7. **Animation.js** - Animation System\n- **Role**: Provides tweening and particle effects\n- **Key Classes**: `TweenManager`, `ParticleSystem`, easing functions\n- **Features**:\n  - Smooth tile movements with various easing functions\n  - Particle explosions for tile removals\n  - Floating score text\n\n### Game Architecture Overview\n\nThe game follows a clean architecture pattern with clear separation of concerns:\n\n```\nGame (Controller)\n├── Board (Data Model)\n├── MatchEngine (Logic)\n├── Renderer (View)\n├── InputHandler (Input)\n├── ScoreSystem (Game Rules)\n└── Animation (Effects)\n```\n\n### Key Game Systems\n\n#### 1. **Board/Matching System**\n- 8x8 grid with 6 colored tiles (apple red, banana yellow, blueberry blue, lime green, grape purple, orange)\n- Matches of 3+ tiles trigger removal\n- L/T shaped matches create area bombs\n- 4 matches create striped bombs (horizontal/vertical)\n- 5 matches create rainbow tiles\n- Cascading matches continue until no more matches\n\n#### 2. **Scoring System**\n- Base score: 10 points per tile removed\n- Chain multipliers: 1x (1 chain), 1.5x (2 chains), 2x (3 chains), 2.5x (4+ chains)\n- Combo text feedback for chains\n- Star rating based on score thresholds\n\n#### 3. **Game Loop Flow**\n```\nIDLE → Input Swap → SWAPPING → Match Detection → MATCHING\n    ↓\nTile Removal → REMOVING → Special Effects → DROPPING\n    ↓\nGravity Apply → Check New Matches → If matches: repeat\n    ↓\nNo More Matches → Check Level Goals → RESULT\n```\n\n#### 4. **Special Tile System**\n- **Striped Bombs**: Remove entire row or column\n- **Area Bombs**: Remove 3x3 area around tile\n- **Rainbow Tiles**: Remove all tiles of one color\n- Special tiles are created during matches and triggered on next move\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n- **Rendering**: Pure Canvas 2D with pixel ratio support\n- **Input**: Touch and mouse event handling with swipe detection\n- **Animation**: Custom tween system with multiple easing functions\n- **Particles**: Custom particle system for visual effects\n- **Performance**: Optimized for 60fps with minimal draw calls\n- **Platform**: Designed for Douyin Mini Game platform (HTML5/CSS3/JS)\n\nThe codebase is well-structured, modular, and implements core match-3 mechanics with room for expansion (obstacles, special goals, social features as outlined in GDD.md). The architecture supports easy addition of new features while maintaining clean separation of concerns."}],"totalDurationMs":169511,"totalTokens":75566,"totalToolUseCount":15,"usage":{"input_tokens":356,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":72910,"output_tokens":2300,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"